Supported RADOS backend scope:
==============================

The backend supports archive, retrieve, list, axes, wipe, control (lock/unlock), and reopening
catalogues by URI. Operations on a single RadosStore instance must be serialised by the caller; separate writer
instances can archive concurrently to the same database. Catalogue-side purge, move, mount,
overlay, and the statistics visitor (fdb-stats) are not implemented.

RADOS placement is configured on `spaces[].roots[]`; legacy `rados.pool`, `rados.root_namespace`,
and `rados.namespace_prefix` values are not used. The first matching space must have exactly one
root with all of these required attributes:

```yaml
spaces:
- regex: ".*"
  roots:
  - pool: fdb-rados
    root_namespace: fdb-root
    namespace_prefix: fdb
```

- `pool` is the Ceph pool for the selected space.
- `root_namespace` holds the space's `main_kv` registry, which maps database namespaces to catalogue URIs.
- `namespace_prefix` forms each database namespace: a DB key with values `11:22` is stored in
    `fdb_11:22`. It must not contain `_`, the prefix/key separator.

The catalogue KV is `rados:fdb-rados/fdb_11:22/catalogue_kv`; index (`index.*`), axis (`axis.*`) and
data (`data.*`) objects share the `fdb_11:22` namespace. Multiple spaces may share a pool when their root namespaces and namespace
prefixes are distinct.

Build and test:
===============

RADOS tests require eckit to be built with RADOS support and a reachable Ceph cluster.

cmake <bundle-source> -DENABLE_RADOS=ON -DENABLE_RADOSFDB=ON -DFDB_RADOS_TEST_POOL=<existing pool>
ctest -L rados

See docs/fdb/content/rados-backend.rst for the layout, configuration and limitations.
